  "id": "organizational-culture",
  "term": "organizational culture",
  "definition": "Organizational culture is the set of shared values, beliefs, and behavior patterns that shape how people in an institution interact and what is expected of them. In workplace settings, it can influence commitment, morale, psychological safety, and whether people feel aligned with the organization or want to leave it.",
